          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "description": "Chiapas: Ardea alba egretta, Apr. 1943 (Zavaleta 1944); Habia rubica, Apr. 1942 (Zavaleta 1944). Distrito Federal: Bombycilla cedrorum, Pueblo de Santa Rosa, Suroeste de la Ciudad de Mexico, sobre los kilómetros 27 – 31 de la carretera al Desierto de los Leones (Zavaleta 1943 a). Notes: Specimens of C. decimfasciatus were identified by Zavaleta (1943 a; 1944) as “ Colpocephalum laticeps K. ”, and by Klaas (1968) as “ Ciconiphilus obscurus (Giebel, 1874) ”. Records from Bombycilla cedrorum and Habia rubica are most likely the result of contaminations because C. decimfasciatus is a regular and natural parasite of herons, family Ardeidae (see Price et al. 2003).",
